Over the next few weeks, socialist, communist and anarchist militias were crushed by the army and Alfonso XIII was pardoned.

@victory
view-if: ejercito_loyalty >= 0.35 or guardia_civil_loyalty >= 0.5 or assault_guard_formed = 1 
on-arrival: ejercito_loyalty += 0.1; guardia_civil_loyalty += 0.05; polarization -= 10; pro_republic += 10

In the aftermath, the Guardia Civil stops being an independent organ to be under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Gobernación, 109 newspapers were closed, 5.000 collaborators were imprisoned and their rural estates are open to nationalization without reparations. 

Sanjurjo was condemned to death penalty for treason, but he was finally condemned to life sentence with a decree of the President of the Republic. 
